WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.404
 Colt and Scott,
in this competition

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:07.606
we were inspired by
history's legends.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:10.442
Now we ask that you continue
to be inspired by history's

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:12.545
legends as we send
you back to your home

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.014
forge to make one of these.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.819
Excalibur!

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:22.588
It's actually not Excalibur.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:26.725
The sword in the stone
is a medieval broadsword.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:27.660
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.628
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.536
SCOTT: Today, I'm making
a European broadsword.

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:39.539
I'm going to do two
types of twisted masses

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:45.044
going opposite directions and
a linear bar for the center.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.146
I am very happy to be back home.

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:49.382
I know that I have all the
proper tooling to do stuff very

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.751
quickly, but I think
it's going to be

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:53.886
a very challenging competition.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.187
It's the end of day one.

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:58.591
I got the twisted masses done.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.960
I've got to cut them to size
and then clean up the edges

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.928
that I'm going to reweld.

00:01:03.028 --> 00:01:05.999 line:7%
That's where it's at right now.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.434
 I'm feeling pretty nervous
going into the clench,

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.603
really hoping I don't
get any warps or cracks.

00:01:17.676 --> 00:01:18.878
Oh, [bleep].

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.746
COLT: It's taken a warp.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:22.448
I'm really struggling here.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.885
I'm bending it, seeing
if it will straighten.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.120
I'm heating it up with
a torch and trying

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.990
to drop water droplets
on it to see if I

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:34.894
can set it back into shape.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:38.331
I finally get this warp out
by taking my pair of tongs

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:41.634
and pushing down on the sword.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.169
That straightened
it out a little bit.

00:01:44.269 --> 00:01:46.239 line:0%
Trying to fix the warp
really set me back,

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:49.642 line:0%
but tomorrow I'm going to
come in with a fresh mind

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:52.645 line:7%
and see what I can get done.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.180 line:0%
SCOTT: Yesterday was
really productive.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.915 line:0%
I got the three
bars of Damascus put

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:59.219 line:0%
together, forged out to a sword,
and then I got it ground down.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.521
Today's most important thing is
getting that heat treat done.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.990
If I can get it done early,
I can focus on the handle

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:04.791
for the rest of the build.

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:14.433
It's pretty straight, and
it definitely heat treated.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.037
I'm just going to clamp
it while it cools.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:20.039
I thought I had the
heat treat right,

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.642
but unfortunately
after I pull it out,

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.942
it's got a nice warp in it.

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:24.677
Oh, [bleep].

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:29.549
It looks like I might
have to heat treat again.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:32.886
The one difference is I'm
going to use my quench tank

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.386
as my temper oil.

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:36.355
I'm going to get the oil
up to the same temperatures

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:39.558
as I would the oven,
to about 450 degrees,

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:42.228
then hold my sword in it
for at least 10 minutes

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.696
so it gets a nice soak.

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:51.170
Pull it out of the quench, and
it comes out almost perfect.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.706 line:0%
All I have to do tomorrow
is fit and finish,

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.641 line:7%
guard, handle, pommel.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:03:00.112 line:0%
COLTON: The theme of day
three is handles and guards.

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:01.980
All that needs to
be done is etching

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:04.050
and sharpening on the blade.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:07.153
I'm going to acid etch
the blade now, let it

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:09.555
sit in there for a few minutes.

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:14.661
So the top of the blade
is not hardened as much

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.995
as I would like it to be.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.796
I want to make
sure that it's not

00:03:17.896 --> 00:03:19.532
going to take a bend or a set.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.403
It seems to have
held up pretty well,

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:29.342
so the last thing I need
to do is the handle.

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.210
It's the end of day three.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.712
I have the finished blade.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.313
I've got the guard fit up.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.415
The handle is shaped
like I want it.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:41.187 line:0%
All I have left to do is
the pommel, and it's done.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.056 line:0%
SCOTT: Beginning of day
four, I'm ready to get

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.490 line:7%
the sword finished.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:47.259
First I need to get
the holes drilled

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:51.063
on the guard and the pommel.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.131
And that's all I need.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.299
It's looking pretty good.

00:03:54.399 --> 00:03:57.669
End of day four, this
broadsword is built,

00:03:57.736 --> 00:04:01.174
and I am ready to go
have dinner with my wife.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:04.477
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.879
It's time to get medieval
on your broadsword.

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:10.149
I'm going to take your weapons,
deliver some slashes and blows

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.051
on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.052
Colton, you're up first.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:13.952
You ready for this?

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:14.687
 Yeah.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.555
 Let's have fun.

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:19.058
COLTON: I'm feeling
confident about my sword,

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:22.228
but I really don't know
what could go wrong.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:25.031
I've never made a sword before.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:32.605
[music playing]

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:50.789
 That thing was sharp.

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:53.659
DOUG: All right, Colton,
first up, I really appreciate

00:04:53.725 --> 00:04:55.460
the balance you have
with this because it's

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:58.364
easy to wield with forward
slashes, back hands,

00:04:58.464 --> 00:04:59.999
and thrusting with it.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.600
Your edge is sharp.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:04.336
Now your handle, it's
just a little bit too tall

00:05:04.436 --> 00:05:06.305
for me in the tense
of it's wider here.

00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:08.641
But I can still get
a good grip on it,

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:11.377
and more importantly, this
sword, with its balance,

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.711
it will kill.

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:13.680
 Thank you.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:14.580
 All right, Scott.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:15.748
It's your turn, sir.
You ready?

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:16.416
 Yes, sir.

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.284
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:21.620
 I'm ecstatic to see
Doug playing with my sword

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.522
because it's
exciting to see what

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.992
it can do to the human
body, what it's built for.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:34.934
[music playing]

00:05:54.319 --> 00:05:55.654
 All right, Scott.

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:58.991
First up, that is
beautiful to look at.

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:00.359
 Thank you.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.228
DOUG: Now the wire wrap
does give me some kind

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:04.063
of contours to hold onto.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.166
Every slice-- or
should I say chop--

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.701
dug deep into this
ballistics dummy.

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:14.340
Overall, the kind of weapon and
damage you can do with this,

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:15.307
it will kill.

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:16.008
 Thank you.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:21.347
 All right, gentlemen.

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:22.648
It's time for the strength test.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.750
Now to test the strength
and overall construction

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:30.589
of your blades, we have
the battering-ram chop.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:31.557
Colton, you're up first.

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:32.758
You ready?
- All right.

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:33.593
 OK.

00:06:36.495 --> 00:06:39.799
 I'm worried that my
blade is almost too light.

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:44.036
I made this blade for slicing,
not chopping trees down.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.944
[music playing]

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:17.470
 So Colton, there's
some definite issues

00:07:17.536 --> 00:07:19.538
in the heat treat.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:23.375
Right here at the guard,
you picked up a bend,

00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:24.276
and it's not a warp.

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:26.379
This sword is now bent.

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:28.681
And also up here where
the sword is the thinnest

00:07:28.747 --> 00:07:30.783
right at the end of the fuller.

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:33.986
It's a beautiful piece,
but that's a major problem.

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:41.560
 That's severe.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:44.096
 Does it feel like it
could continue testing?

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:45.564
 I wouldn't.

00:07:45.664 --> 00:07:47.132
 I mean, it's like a gun
barrel that's already curved.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:49.668
I don't want to fire something
like that if it's not extreme.

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:51.904
If it's here, it's one
thing, but it's all the way.

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.339
It starts at the handle.

00:07:53.405 --> 00:07:55.741
 Yeah, I mean, it's already
failed as far as I'm concerned.

00:07:55.807 --> 00:07:58.478
 I'm seeing the judges talking,
and it's nerve wracking.

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:03.081
 All right, Colton, there's
a problem with your blade.

00:08:03.148 --> 00:08:06.118
The judges have given your
blade a vote of no confidence.

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:07.552
In other words,
it held together,

00:08:07.652 --> 00:08:10.022
but it's not safe to
move forward in testing.

00:08:10.088 --> 00:08:13.158
That doesn't mean that
you've lost this competition.

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:17.296
Scott, your blade still has to
hold up in this strength test.

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:18.030
Dave?

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:22.467
SCOTT: I am very nervous.

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:23.836
I am very, very nervous.

00:08:23.903 --> 00:08:25.438
I don't know how
it's going to do.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:29.441
All I can do is trust
that I built it correctly.

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:34.046
[music playing]

00:08:49.127 --> 00:08:53.299
 So right off, Scott,
everything's solid and tight.

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:55.066
All in all, I think
you did a great job.

00:08:55.133 --> 00:08:55.768
Nicely done.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:56.536
 Thank you.

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:03.942
 Colton, unfortunately for
you, this means that your blade

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:06.445
doesn't make the cut, and you
cannot be the "Forged in Fire"

00:09:06.512 --> 00:09:08.014
champion.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.615
For that reason, I'd like to
invite you to shake our hands,

00:09:09.682 --> 00:09:12.184
shake Scott's hand, and
then please leave the forge.

00:09:12.251 --> 00:09:13.485
Come on forward, my friend.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:14.787
How old are you?

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:15.654
 18.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.556
 Hey, man, the world's yours.

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:21.626
 I knew the bend could
have possibly happened.

00:09:21.726 --> 00:09:25.898
He outperformed me,
and that's OK with me.

00:09:25.998 --> 00:09:27.332
I can be outdone.

00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:28.099
Good job.

00:09:28.166 --> 00:09:29.335
 Thank you.

00:09:29.435 --> 00:09:30.936
 I might not have
worn "Forged in Fire,"

00:09:31.036 --> 00:09:33.906
but I have learned so
much as a bladesmith,

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:39.244
and I have grown as a person
doing this competition.

00:09:39.311 --> 00:09:40.579
 Scott, congratulations.

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:42.247
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:42.347 --> 00:09:46.251
and that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:46.318 --> 00:09:46.952
Good job, my friend.

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:47.486
[applause]

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:49.322
 Thank you.

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:51.090
 Come on forward.

00:09:51.157 --> 00:09:52.258
Excellent.
- Thank you.

00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:53.058
SCOTT: I won.

00:09:53.158 --> 00:09:54.860
My blade survived.

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:58.797
I feel ecstatic, amazed,
however you want to say.

00:09:58.897 --> 00:10:04.370
I hope that by doing this, I
can go full-time bladesmithing.

